        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "f019d67a-47be-5791-ab90-f6f55ce9ba02",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: John Clare, Jonathan Bate, Matthew Allen\n- Organizations: University of Oxford, Worcester College Oxford, Warwick Business School\n- Places: High Beach\n- Works: The Quickening Maze\n- Topics: English literature, labouring-class poetry, mental asylums\n\nFacts:\n- In the late 1830s and 1840s, Matthew Allen ran a mental asylum at High Beach, and English poet John Clare was admitted there.\n- The Quickening Maze is based on the historical setting of Matthew Allen’s mental asylum at High Beach in the late 1830s and 1840s, where John Clare was a patient.\n- Jonathan Bate is Professor of English Literature at the University of Oxford, Provost of Worcester College, Oxford, and Honorary Fellow of Creativity at Warwick Business School.\n- Jonathan Bate, a biographer of John Clare, stated that John Clare was \"the greatest labouring-class poet that England has ever produced.\"",
